## PostgreSQL Flexible Server

### Creation

#### Production access prerequisites

For production access, create the required Entra groups and access packages before creating or updating the PostgreSQL Flexible Server Terraform. Follow [Create access groups and packages](#create-access-groups-and-packages).

#### Create the server

Create PostgreSQL Flexible Server instances with the [terraform-module-postgresql-flexible](https://github.com/hmcts/terraform-module-postgresql-flexible) module.

Use the module README for the current inputs, examples and operational guidance.

### Production access

This section describes how to self-service the creation of access request packages for PostgreSQL database read and write access.

#### Overview

JIT database access uses Microsoft Entra groups, access packages and the [PostgreSQL Flexible Server Terraform module](https://github.com/hmcts/terraform-module-postgresql-flexible).

For production databases, the group names must match the PostgreSQL flexible server Terraform module naming convention:

- Read access: `DTS JIT Access <product> DB Reader SC`
- Write access: `DTS JIT Access <product> DB Writer SC`

The access package grants membership of the matching group for a limited time. The database Terraform then maps that group to a PostgreSQL role and grants the database permissions.

#### Create access groups and packages

Create the required Entra groups and access packages before creating or updating the PostgreSQL Flexible Server Terraform.

Create whichever access levels the service needs. Write access should only be created and enabled where it is needed and approved.

- Reader group: `DTS JIT Access <product> DB Reader SC`
- Writer group: `DTS JIT Access <product> DB Writer SC`

For each group:

1. Create the group in [azure-access users/groups.yml](https://github.com/hmcts/azure-access/blob/master/users/groups.yml).
2. Add the group to the `Databases` catalog in [azure-access-packages entitlement-catalogs.yml](https://github.com/hmcts/azure-access-packages/blob/master/entitlement-catalogs.yml).
3. Add the access package in [azure-access-packages entitlement-packages.yml](https://github.com/hmcts/azure-access-packages/blob/master/entitlement-packages.yml), following the [azure-access-packages README](https://github.com/hmcts/azure-access-packages#adding-a-new-access-package).

Choose a requestor group that requires security clearance, such as `DTS CFT SC`.

Example pull requests:

- [Create the Entra group in azure-access](https://github.com/hmcts/azure-access/pull/7874/changes)
- [Create the access package in azure-access-packages](https://github.com/hmcts/azure-access-packages/pull/134)

#### Read access

Reader group access is enabled by default with `enable_read_only_group_access = true`, so the reader group must already exist unless `enable_read_only_group_access = false` is set.

If the database needs read access outside the `public` schema, configure `schemas_for_reader_access` in the service infrastructure. See the [PostgreSQL Flexible Server module access documentation](https://github.com/hmcts/terraform-module-postgresql-flexible#access-to-databases).

#### Write access

Only enable write access where it is needed and approved. Enable writer grants in the service infrastructure with `enable_write_group_access = true`.

If write access should apply outside the `public` schema, configure `schemas_for_writer_access` in the service infrastructure. If `schemas_for_writer_access` is not set, the module uses `schemas_for_reader_access`, or `["public"]` if neither value is set.

#### Request read or write access

Before requesting production database access, make sure you are a member of `DTS CFT Developers` or `DTS SDS Developers` and have completed the [security clearance access package](../../onboarding/person/entra-id.html#security-clearance-access-package).

1. Go to [My Access access packages](https://myaccess.microsoft.com/@CJSCommonPlatform.onmicrosoft.com#/access-packages).
2. Search for the database package:
   - Read access: `Database - <product> read access - self approval`
   - Write access: `Database - <product> write access - self approval`
3. Request the package and provide the Jira or Halo link requested in the form.
4. Wait for the access assignment to complete. You may need to sign out and sign in again before your new group membership appears in your Azure PostgreSQL access token.
5. Connect to the database by following the [PostgreSQL flexible server access instructions](https://github.com/hmcts/terraform-module-postgresql-flexible#access-to-databases).
